@{
    var team = ViewBag.Team as Team;
    var title = ViewBag.Title as string ?? "Practice plan";
    var primary = team?.SafePrimary ?? Team.DefaultPrimary;
    var accent  = team?.SafeAccent  ?? Team.DefaultAccent;
    var palette = HockeyPractice.Infrastructure.Palette.CssVariables(primary, accent);
}
<!DOCTYPE html>
@* A stripped shell for the one page built for paper. No team header, no tab bar, no footer,
   and none of _Layout's four script blocks: nothing here has a form, a tag box, a number
   field or a fixed tab bar to dodge, so shipping them would be ~350 lines of dead weight.

   Also deliberately absent: the web manifest (this must never become a PWA start URL),
   theme-color, apple-touch-icon and viewport-fit=cover — there is no safe-area chrome here.

   THERE IS NO VIEW BEACON HERE, AND THAT IS THE DECISION, NOT AN OVERSIGHT. The rule
   everywhere else is that a bounce is not a view, and opening a print preview is the
   definition of not having read the plan. Dedupe would not save it either: PlanView is unique
   on (PlanId, PlayerId), so a beacon here would not double-count, it would falsely FIRST-count
   — a player who printed without reading would show as seen on the coach's roster. Managers
   short-circuit the beacon anyway, so every difference would land on players, in the wrong
   direction. Nothing is lost: Print is reached from Details, which recorded the view already.

   The team palette still rides on <html>, because the drill number badge and the running-order
   clock resolve --hp-primary-text; without it every team prints in the fallback blue. The
   hp-printpage class is on <html> rather than <body> so the print stylesheet can scope
   root-level rules — the font size and the colour tokens — to this page alone, leaving Ctrl+P
   on every other page exactly as it was. *@
<html lang="en" class="hp-printpage" style="@palette">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>@title</title>
    @* This sheet is a full duplicate of Plan/Details at its own URL and with the same title, so
       without this a crawler that ever reached one would have two copies of the same practice to
       choose between. Nothing here is linked publicly, but noindex costs one line and does not
       depend on that staying true. *@
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/hockeypractice.css" asp-append-version="true" />
    <link rel="icon" href="~/favicon.ico" sizes="16x16 32x32 48x48" asp-append-version="true" />
</head>
<body>
    @* Same main landmark as _Layout. No skip link: this layout has no chrome to skip. *@
    <main>
        @RenderBody()
    </main>
    @await RenderSectionAsync("Scripts", required: false)
</body>
</html>
